/// An identifier may contain a Unicode letter from outside the Latin scripts.
///
/// Separate from CharsUnicodeLatin because the two can be fixed apart and often
/// are.  Latin-1 letters are two bytes each in UTF-8; these are two and three,
/// and Greek carries a case pairing (Δ/δ) while Han carries none at all.  A fix
/// that widens the scanner's alphabet byte-wise passes the Latin file and fails
/// this one.
///
/// The case pairing here is deliberate.  If identifier case is ever folded, the
/// fold has to cover this range too -- see 'Identifier case' in ALGOL-24.md --
/// and a Greek name is the cheapest place for that to show up.  This test does
/// not assert the fold; it only puts the character where a fold would meet it.
///
/// Fails with: [line N] Error: Unexpected character: <byte>  (no test ran)
///
test 'An identifier may contain a Greek or Han letter';
begin
    var Δelta : Integer := 1;
    var 半径  : Integer := 2;

    AssertEqual (1, Δelta);
    AssertEqual (2, 半径);
end
